# bedrock-strands-agent

FastAPI + Strands Agents extraction service over Amazon Bedrock. Hot
path: PDF / image / text → schema-validated JSON with field-level
confidence and citation excerpts.

Detailed onboarding lives in [`AGENTS.md`](mdc:AGENTS.md). This rule
captures the must-know basics so they are loaded into every chat.

## Commands

- `uv run pytest` — full suite (coverage gate 85%, set in `pyproject.toml`)
- `uv run ruff check src tests` — lint
- `uv run ruff format <file>` then `uv run ruff check --fix <file>`
  after every Python edit (Cursor has no PostToolUse hook; do this
  manually before declaring a change done)
- `uv run mypy src` — strict typecheck
- `uv add <pkg>` to add deps; never edit `uv.lock` directly

## Branch model

`main` and `dev` are **protected**. Direct push is forbidden. Land
every change via merge/pull request from a feature branch
(`feat/...`, `fix/...`, `chore/...`). Standard target is `dev`.

## Files you must NOT edit

- `uv.lock` — managed by `uv add` / `uv lock`
- `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.<env>`, `.env.<env>.local` — secrets;
  `.env.example` is the only `.env*` file that's checked in and
  editable

If a change requires a `.env` template update, edit `.env.example`
instead.

## When to invoke specialised rules

Cursor auto-attaches these by glob:

- Any change under `src/bedrock_strands_agent/{extraction,api,logging,telemetry}.py`
  → security-pii rule fires (`@security-pii`).
- Any change under `src/bedrock_strands_agent/templates/*.j2`
  → prompt-templates rule fires (`@prompt-templates`).

These rules encode the same invariants the Claude `security-reviewer`
and `prompt-template-reviewer` subagents enforce on Claude Code.

